    "lyrics": "[Intro - Male Rapper 1]\nYeah\nNewt World outside\nBackpacks ready\nCameras ready\nLet’s hit the road\n[Female Hook - Bright, Addictive]\nNewt World, let’s go\nDown the road, nice and slow\nCreek side, moonlight\nFind a little life tonight\nNewt World, come on\nFrom the sunset to the dawn\nGreen woods, clear sky\nWe’re going wild tonight\n[Verse 1 - Male Rapper 1, Laid-Back Storytelling]\nSaturday, eight in the morning\nGroup chat says everybody’s coming\nCoffee in one hand, boots in the back\nCamera batteries, loaded and packed\nOne car, two cars, meet at the spot\nSomebody’s late — yeah, of course, why not?\nWindows down, music turned up\nHalf awake but we’re laughing too much\nCity gets smaller, trees get tall\nPhone signal drops, we don’t care at all\nPull off the road by a little old trail\nCold running water and leaves on the rail\nWalk real slow, watch where you step\nLook by the rocks where the ground stays wet\nThen somebody whispers, “Yo, right there”\nLittle newt moving like it owns the place\n[Female Hook]\nNewt World, let’s go\nDown the road, nice and slow\nCreek side, moonlight\nFind a little life tonight\nNewt World, come on\nFrom the sunset to the dawn\nGreen woods, clear sky\nWe’re going wild tonight\n[Verse 2 - Male Rapper 2, Brighter Playful Flow]\nKeep moving down by the waterline\nTiny green frog on a leaf — good find\nEverybody stops, everybody stares\nTen grown people acting like millionaires\nCamera comes out, get the angle right\nNobody move, let it sit there tight\nTake a few shots, then we back away\nLeave everything exactly where it stayed\nNext little pond and the sun goes low\nFlashlights on, now we’re moving slow\nOne salamander underneath a log\nThen three more frogs by the edge of the bog\nMud on the shoes, rain on the coat\nSomebody slipped — man, there goes my Coke\nNobody cares, we’re having a blast\nWhole day gone and it went way too fast\n[Female Hook]\nNewt World, let’s go\nDown the road, nice and slow\nCreek side, moonlight\nFind a little life tonight\nNewt World, come on\nFrom the sunset to the dawn\nGreen woods, clear sky\nWe’re going wild tonight\n[Bridge - Male Rapper 1]\nNo cages, no taking them home\nThis is their place, we’re just passing through\nTake a picture, take a memory\nThen leave the wild the way we found it too\n[Bridge - Male Rapper 2]\nDifferent towns, different lives\nBut today we’re side by side\nNewts and frogs and salamanders\nThat’s a pretty good day in my eyes\n[Final Hook - Female Vocal, Bigger]\nNewt World, let’s go\nDown the road, nice and slow\nCreek side, moonlight\nFind a little life tonight\nNewt World, come on\nFrom the sunset to the dawn\nGreen woods, clear sky\nWe’re going wild tonight\n[Male Ad-libs]\nWatch your step!\nOver here!\nI found one!\nGet the camera!\nNewt World!\n[Final Hook - Female Vocal]\nNewt World, let’s go\nDown the road, nice and slow\nCreek side, moonlight\nFind a little life tonight\nNewt World, come on\nFrom the sunset to the dawn\nGreen woods, clear sky\nWe’re going wild tonight\n[Outro - Male Rapper 1 + Female Vocal]\nDirty shoes\nMemory cards full\nLong ride home\nGood day\n[Female]\nNewt World, let’s go\nWe’ll do it all again\n[Female]\nNewt World, let’s go\nWe’ll do it all again",
